cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Decision Topology: A Framework for Ethics Under Irreversibility"
version: "1.3"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
authors:
  - family-names: Shunan
    given-names: Yusuf Abdulla
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://yusufshunan.com
repository-code: https://github.com/yusuf/decision-topology
abstract: >
  Decision Topology is a minimal, operational ethics framework for
  decision-making under irreversibility. It defines impermissible action
  in terms of non-participatory closure of agent futures and provides
  structured protocols applicable to personal, institutional, policy,
  and AI contexts.
keywords:
  - ethics
  - decision-making
  - irreversibility
  - consent
  - agency
  - AI ethics
  - governance

